---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Find your belt size"><article class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE GUIDE TO A GREAT FIT</p><h1>Measure once.<br/>Wear it every day.</h1><p>The best guide is a belt you already love. Measure from the buckle pin to the hole you use most. That measurement is your belt size, not the total length of the strap.</p><h2>A good starting point.</h2><p>Choose a belt about 2 inches larger than your trouser waist. Fit varies by rise, clothing and personal preference, so use this as a guide and confirm the measurement.</p><form id="size-calc"><label for="waist">Your waist measurement</label><div class="inline-form"><input id="waist" type="number" min="18" max="152" step="0.1" required placeholder="e.g. 32"/><select id="waist-unit" aria-label="Measurement unit"><option value="in">Inches</option><option value="cm">Centimetres</option></select><button class="btn">Find my size</button></div><p id="size-result" role="status"></p></form><h2>The three small steps.</h2><ol><li>Wrap a measuring tape where your belt will sit, over your trousers.</li><li>Keep it comfortably snug, without pulling tight.</li><li>Add about 2 inches and choose the closest available size. If between sizes, size up.</li></ol><p>For kids, measure an existing belt or the waist over clothing. Gift sets include the belt sizes listed on their product page. Width is shown in millimetres; check your trouser loops before choosing.</p></article></Layout>
